.TH STAT 2
.SH NAME
stat, fstat \- get file status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <sys/types.h>"
.B "#include <sys/stat.h>"
.sp
.B "stat(name, buf)"
.B "char *name;"
.B "struct stat *buf;"
.sp
.B "fstat(fildes, buf)"
.B "struct stat *buf;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stat
obtains detailed information about a named file.
.B fstat
obtains the
same information about an open file known by the file descriptor from a
successful
.BR open ,
.BR creat ,
.BR dup ,
or
.BR pipe (2)
call.
.PP
.I name
points to a null-terminated string naming a file;
.I buf
is the address
of a buffer into which information is placed concerning the file.
It is
unnecessary to have any permissions at all with respect to the file, but all
directories leading to the file must be searchable.
The layout of the structure
pointed to by
.I buf
as defined in
.B <sys/stat.h>
is given below.
.B st_mode
is encoded according to the ``#define'' statements.
.PP
.nf
.ta .7i 1.5i 2.3i
struct	stat
{
	dev_t	st_dev;
	ino_t	st_ino;
	unsigned short	st_mode;
	short	st_nlink;
	short	st_uid;
	short	st_gid;
	dev_t	st_rdev;
	off_t	st_size;
	time_t	st_atime;
	time_t	st_mtime;
	time_t	st_ctime;
};
.fi
.PP
The meaning of each element is:
.PD 0
.TP 1.2i
.B st_dev
major/minor number of device this file is on
.TP
.B st_ino
inode number of this file
.TP
.B st_mode
file mode (see encoding below)
.TP
.B st_uid
owner ID number
.TP
.B st_gid
group ID number
.TP
.B st_rdev
if this is a special file (device), major/minor number of
device it points to
.TP
.B st_size
length in bytes
.TP
.B st_atime
last accessed time (for reasons of efficiency, this is not set
when a directory is searched, although this would be
more logical)
.TP
.B st_mtime
last modified time
.TP
.B st_ctime
currently the same as
.B st_mtime
.PD
.PP
The bit encoding of
.B st_mode
is
.PP
.nf
.ta .8i 1.8i 2.7i
#define	S_IFMT	0160000	/* type of file */
#define	S_IFDIR	0140000	/* directory */
#define	S_IFCHR	0120000	/* character special */
#define	S_IFBLK	0160000	/* block special */
#define	S_IFREG	0100000	/* regular */
#define	S_ILRG	0010000	/* large file */
#define	S_ISUID	0004000	/* set user id on execution */
#define	S_ISGID	0002000	/* set group id on execution */
#define	S_ISVTX	0001000	/* save shared even after use */
#define	S_IREAD	0000400	/* read permission, owner */
#define	S_IWRITE	0000200	/* write permission, owner */
#define	S_IEXEC	0000100	/* execute/search permission */
.fi
.PP
The mode bits 0000070 and 0000007 encode group and others permissions
(see
.BR chmod (2)).
.PP
The defined types,
.BR ino_t ,
.BR off_t ,
.BR time_t ,
name various width integer
values;
.B dev_t
encodes major and minor device numbers; their exact
definitions are in the include file <sys/types.h> (see
.BR types (5)).
.PP
When
.I fildes
is associated with a pipe,
.B fstat
reports an ordinary file with
restricted permissions.
The size is the number of bytes queued in the
pipe.
.PP
Note that the stat buffer format differs from the disk inode format.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ls(1), filsys(4)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Zero is returned if a status is available; \-1 if the file cannot be found.
.SH ASSEMBLER
(stat = 18.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys stat; name; buf
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 18
AX = name
DX = buf
int 0Xf1
.fi
.PP
(fstat = 28.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0 = file descriptor
sys fstat; buf
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 28
AX = buf
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
